  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that multimodal multiprofile configurations with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion (e.g., config_019) achieve high accuracy. This experiment tests whether replacing the RNA encoder (scvi_n200 → scgpt) and image encoder (imagenet_vit_l → resnet50) while retaining transformer aggregation and weighted fusion affects performance. It isolates the impact of encoder choices on performance, which is critical for understanding design trade-offs, while building on the promising direction of multiprofile and transformer-based models."
